SUMMARY:The Southern Highland Craft Guild's 46th Annual Heritage Weekend
DESCRIPTION:You are invited to our 46th. annual Heritage Weekend on September 19 and 20 at the Folk Art Center on the Blue Ridge Parkway. \nMany of you have been to this fun event in the past and we will again host over 20 heritage artist\, musicians and dancers to honor and celebrate Mountain Heritage Crafts. \nOne of the highlights of the celebration is our Annual World Gee Haw Whimmy Diddle competition on Saturday afternoon. \nA Whimmy Diddle is an Appalachian mountain toy\, traditionally made from 2 sticks  of rhododendron. Notches are carved into the stick and a propeller is attached to the end. Rubbing the notches with the second stick makes the propeller spin! The trick is to make it spin gee (to the right) or haw (to the left). \nContestants are judged by their skills and interesting prizes will be awarded. \nThe music stage will provide entertainment with Blue Grass and Gospel music\, and cloggers will demonstrate the mountain dance tradition. \n\n\n\nFolk Art Center\, Blue Ridge Parkway\n\n\nCome for the craft\, stay for the music!\n\n\n\n\nEntertainment Schedule: \nLive Bluegrass and Mountain Music performances on an outdoor stage\n\nSaturday\, Sept. 19 \n10 a.m. – Ash Woody- Appalachian Jack Tales\n11 a.m. – Michael and Donna Fox \n12 p.m.- Blue-Eyed Girl\n1 p.m. – Split Rail\n2 p.m. – 46th Annual World Gee Haw Whimmy Diddle Competition\n3 p.m. – Carol Rifkin and Friends \nSunday\, Sept. 20\n11 a.m. – Davy Arch- Cherokee Stories\n12 p.m. – Nobody’s Darlin’ Stringband\n1 p.m. – Jonah Riddle and Carolina Express\n2 p.m. – Buncombe Turnpike\n3 p.m. – Janet Wiseman and Pearl Shirley – Mountain Music
URL:https://livemusicasheville.com/calendar/heritage-weekend-2/2026-09-19/
LOCATION:Folk Art Center\, Blue Ridge Parkway
CATEGORIES:Asheville Area,Live Music
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://livemusicasheville.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/799773895_1079489951705543_5534703578023715376_n-e1789405354556.jpg
END:VEVENT
